# eCL API token — template. THIS FILE IS TRACKED IN GIT; the real one is not.
#
#   cp .ecl_token.example .ecl_token
#   chmod 600 .ecl_token
#   # then replace the placeholder line at the bottom with your token
#
# Where to get it
# ---------------
# Self-service, no approval needed: open
#
#     https://ecl.cyberlink.com/sso/mgm/tokenPage
#
# and issue a personal API token. The same token works for every TR / eBug
# endpoint. No VPN required — ecl.cyberlink.com is reachable externally, but
# you do have to pass eCL SSO login. (The Client ID / Secret you request from
# Jeffy Chuang are a different thing entirely: those are for the eCL *MCP*
# connector, not for this REST token.)
#
# How it is found
# ---------------
# $ECL_TOKEN  >  $ECL_TOKEN_FILE  >  this directory's .ecl_token  >  ~/.ecl_token
#
# A token here rather than only in ~ means the Jenkins user on the Mac Mini
# reads the same credential as an interactive run, with no second copy.
#
# Handle with care
# ----------------
# Query endpoints have NO permission filtering (guide 3-5): a valid token
# reads every ticket in scope — roughly 242,000 eBugs — including ones you
# could not open in the eCL web UI. It is not equivalent to your web login.
# Do not commit it, paste it into Slack / Teams, or copy it into a shared doc.
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored, so the token is the first real line:
PASTE_YOUR_ECL_TOKEN_HERE
